---
/**
 * About page heading: a small "About" label over an oversized "The Connect
 * Digital". One h1, so it's announced as "About The Connect Digital".
 *
 * Line breaks are set here, never left to the browser:
 *   below md  three stacked lines (The / Connect / Digital), sized so the
 *             longest word fills the width
 *   md and up one line, sized to fill the width
 *
 * Sizing is CSS container units against measured Fraunces widths (optical
 * size fixed at 144, weight 500, tracking -0.03em):
 *   "The Connect Digital" = 7.1866em   "Connect" = 3.0611em
 * with a 2% margin. RE-MEASURE THESE IF THE DISPLAY FACE CHANGES (Fraunces is
 * provisional); the /lab and Phase 5 checks catch any overflow.
 *
 * Revealed by src/lib/headline-reveal.ts ([data-headline]).
 */
---

<div class="wordmark-box">
  <!-- Explicit {' '} spaces: Astro's HTML compression strips whitespace
       between tags, which would make the accessible name "AboutTheConnectDigital". -->
  <h1 id="about-title" class="wordmark" data-headline>
    <span class="wordmark-label">About</span>{' '}
    <span class="wordmark-name">
      <span class="wordmark-line">The</span>{' '}
      <span class="wordmark-line">Connect</span>{' '}
      <span class="wordmark-line">Digital</span>
    </span>
  </h1>
</div>

<style>
  .wordmark-box {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .wordmark {
    text-wrap: nowrap;
  }

  .wordmark-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: var(--text-small--line-height);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .wordmark-name {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 0.9;
    /* Longest word ("Connect", 3.0611em) fills the width, less 2%. */
    font-size: calc(100cqi / 3.0611 * 0.98);
  }

  .wordmark-line {
    display: block;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .wordmark-name {
      /* Whole name (7.1866em) on one line, less 2%. */
      font-size: calc(100cqi / 7.1866 * 0.98);
    }

    .wordmark-line {
      display: inline;
    }
  }
</style>
